1
00:02:24,705 --> 00:02:30,705
A story of two friends who didn't know they were supposed to be enemies.

2
00:04:49,411 --> 00:04:55,411
The Fox and the Hound is a adventure, animation,
drama film directed by Richard Rich.

3
00:07:14,117 --> 00:07:20,117
When a feisty little fox named Tod is adopted into a farm family, he quickly
becomes friends with a fun and adorable hound puppy named Copper.

4
00:09:38,823 --> 00:09:44,823
Life is full of hilarious adventures until Copper is expected to take on his role as
a hunting dog -- and the object of his search is his best friend!

5
00:12:03,529 --> 00:12:09,529
Tod (voice), played by Mickey Rooney.

6
00:14:28,235 --> 00:14:34,235
Copper (voice), played by Kurt Russell.

7
00:16:52,941 --> 00:16:58,941
Big Mama (voice), played by Pearl Bailey.

8
00:19:17,647 --> 00:19:23,647
Amos Slade (voice), played by Jack Albertson.

9
00:21:42,352 --> 00:21:48,352
Vixey (voice), played by Sandy Duncan.

10
00:24:07,058 --> 00:24:13,058
Widow Tweed (voice), played by Jeanette Nolan.

11
00:26:31,764 --> 00:26:37,764
The Fox and the Hound is a 1981 American animated buddy drama film produced by Walt Disney
Productions and loosely based on the 1967 novel of the same name by Daniel P.

12
00:28:56,470 --> 00:29:02,470
It tells the story of the unlikely friendship between a red fox named Tod and a hound named Copper, as they
struggle against their emerging instincts and the realization that they are meant to be adversaries.

13
00:31:21,176 --> 00:31:27,176
The film was directed by Ted Berman, Richard Rich, and Art Stevens.

14
00:33:45,882 --> 00:33:51,882
It was produced by Ron Miller, Wolfgang Reitherman, and Art Stevens.

15
00:36:10,588 --> 00:36:16,588
The ensemble voice cast consists of Mickey Rooney as Tod and Kurt Russell as Copper, respectively, with Pearl Bailey, Jack Albertson (in his final film role), Sandy Duncan, Jeanette
Nolan, Pat Buttram, John Fiedler, John McIntire, Dick Bakalyan, Paul Winchell, Keith Mitchell, and Corey Feldman providing the voices of the other characters of the film.

16
00:38:35,294 --> 00:38:41,294
Mitchell and Feldman in particular voiced Young Tod and Young Copper.

17
00:41:00,000 --> 00:41:06,000
The instrumental musical score to the film was composed and conducted by
Buddy Baker, with Walter Sheets performing the orchestration.

18
00:43:24,705 --> 00:43:30,705
Walt Disney Productions first obtained the film rights to the novel by Daniel P.

19
00:45:49,411 --> 00:45:55,411
Mannix in 1967; however, actual development on the
film would not occur until spring 1977.

20
00:48:14,117 --> 00:48:20,117
It marked the last involvement of the remaining members of Disney's Nine
Old Men, which included Frank Thomas and Ollie Johnston.

21
00:50:38,823 --> 00:50:44,823
Though they had involvement in early development of the film, it was ultimately handed over to
a new generation of animators following the retirement of the old animators.

22
00:53:03,529 --> 00:53:09,529
As such, it was the first film for future directors,
including Tim Burton, Brad Bird, and John Lasseter.

23
00:55:28,235 --> 00:55:34,235
During production, its release was delayed by over six months following the
abrupt departure of Don Bluth and his team of animators.

24
00:57:52,941 --> 00:57:58,941
Further concerns were raised over the handling of the scene in which Chief is hit
by a train, which was originally planned to result in him dying.

25
01:00:17,647 --> 01:00:23,647
After debating the handling of the scene, the filmmakers decided to change the
death into a non-fatal injury by which he merely suffers a broken leg.

26
01:02:42,352 --> 01:02:48,352
The film was released to theaters on July 10, 1981, by Buena Vista Distribution.

27
01:05:07,058 --> 01:05:13,058
It was a financial success, earning $39.9 million
domestically and receiving mixed reviews from critics.

28
01:07:31,764 --> 01:07:37,764
It was nominated for three awards, of which it won one.

29
01:09:56,470 --> 01:10:02,470
At the time of its release, it was the most expensive animated
film produced to date, costing $12 million.

30
01:12:21,176 --> 01:12:27,176
It was re-released to theaters on March 25, 1988.

31
01:14:45,882 --> 01:14:51,882
An intermediate follow-up, The Fox and the Hound 2, was
released directly-to-DVD on December 12, 2006.

32
01:17:10,588 --> 01:17:16,588
The film explores themes of friendship, based on
novel or book, fox, coming of age, dog.

33
01:19:35,294 --> 01:19:41,294
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
